        "original_id": "a8888188-0eaa-5a04-a6a2-a87450f3bb8b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: International Grenfell Association, Corner Brook Transit\n- People: Sir Wilfred Grenfell\n- Places: Newfoundland and Labrador, northern Newfoundland, Labrador, Battle Harbour, Mary's Harbour, Corner Brook\n- Roles: medical missionary\n- Topics: health care, education, religious services, rehabilitation, public transportation\n\nFacts:\n- Sir Wilfred Thomason Grenfell was born on 28 February 1865 and died on 9 October 1940.\n- Sir Wilfred Thomason Grenfell was a medical missionary to Newfoundland and Labrador.\n- Sir Wilfred Grenfell founded the International Grenfell Association.\n- The International Grenfell Association provides health care, education, religious services, rehabilitation, and other social activities to fishermen and coastal communities in northern Newfoundland and along the coast of Labrador.\n- After a fire destroyed its hospital and boarding school in Battle Harbour, the International Grenfell Association decided to relocate them to Mary's Harbour.\n- Corner Brook Transit provides public transportation to residents of Corner Brook, Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada.",
